1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,670
Applying for jobs is a full-time job.

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:07,650
Except it doesn't pay, and it's ninety percent dropdowns.

3
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:10,690
Meet Job Hunter Agent.

4
00:00:10,690 --> 00:00:12,230
It does the boring part.

5
00:00:12,230 --> 00:00:15,090
You stay in charge of the part that matters.

6
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:19,090
Step one: answer the questions every application asks.

7
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:20,510
Once.

8
00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:23,630
Your name, your visa, whether you'd move to New York.

9
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:26,630
Prefer not to say is always an option.

10
00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:29,860
Step two: tell it your story.

11
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:35,100
Type it, say it out loud, or just drop in a résumé you secretly admire.

12
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,340
Say what you like about it, hit Send,

13
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:41,720
and watch it rewrite your storybook in that style, line by line.

14
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:45,480
This storybook is the only thing the agent is allowed to say about you.

15
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:48,390
So, no surprise PhD.

16
00:00:48,870 --> 00:00:49,890
Don't love it?

17
00:00:49,890 --> 00:00:51,770
One click takes you back.

18
00:00:52,370 --> 00:00:57,130
Every morning, it checks the job boards of the companies you care about.

19
00:00:57,130 --> 00:00:58,610
Then it scores every role.

20
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:03,880
Green means go, orange means maybe, and under fifty, it doesn't even bother.

21
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:09,040
Hit Prepare, and it builds a one-page résumé from your storybook.

22
00:01:11,230 --> 00:01:13,300
Then it fills out the actual application.

23
00:01:13,860 --> 00:01:18,860
Names, dropdowns, even those tiny checkboxes nobody reads.

24
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:21,300
And when a form asks why you want to work there,

25
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:25,480
it starts with their mission, not a cover-letter cliché.

26
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:28,200
And then, it stops.

27
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:31,420
Everything waits for you in the review queue.

28
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:36,670
Anything only you can answer shows up right here, with the form's own options.

29
00:01:36,670 --> 00:01:38,580
Nothing goes out until you hit Approve.

30
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:39,960
You're the boss.

31
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:44,390
The agent is the intern who actually read the job description.

32
00:01:45,290 --> 00:01:48,870
If a CAPTCHA or an email code shows up, that one's yours.

33
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:52,920
It's a robot, and it's not allowed to pretend otherwise.

34
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:59,440
After you apply, it reads your inbox, read-only, and moves each application along.

35
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:01,540
Received, next step, interview, offer.

36
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:03,810
Or, you know, the other one.

37
00:02:04,410 --> 00:02:07,450
Under the hood, it's a simple pipeline.

38
00:02:07,450 --> 00:02:09,120
Your storybook goes in.

39
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:14,600
The agent finds roles, ranks them, builds the résumé, and fills the form.

40
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:15,280
You approve.

41
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:18,980
It submits, tracks the replies, and learns from your notes,

42
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:22,280
one small fix at a time, which you approve too.

43
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,010
Job Hunter Agent.

44
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,820
Open source, and on your side.

45
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:28,060
It does the grind.

46
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:29,590
You do the talking.
